cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the associated manuscript, please cite it."
title: "Cross-Split Edge Auditing for Cryptocurrency AML Evaluation: Degree, Composition, and a Pre-Deployment Test"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Han
    given-names: Xiaole
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9611-2368"
    affiliation: "Business School, Qilu Institute of Technology, Jinan, Shandong 250200, China"
abstract: >-
  An audit of evaluation protocols for cryptocurrency anti-money laundering.
  The repository contains the code, results, generated tables, and LaTeX source
  for the manuscript submitted to IEEE TDSC. The central result is that the
  dominant channel of a protocol effect differs by graph: degree on a 1,500-node
  co-occurrence graph, label composition on Elliptic, where no edge crosses a
  time step. The deliverable is a pre-deployment test based on three measurable
  structural quantities.
keywords:
  - anti-money laundering
  - evaluation protocol
  - temporal split
  - data leakage
  - graph neural networks
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hanxiaole666/aml-edge-audit"
version: "v1.1-artifact"
